# ~/.config/environment.d/50-theming.conf — rendered by roles/theming.
#
# Reaches every user unit, including xdg-desktop-portal-gtk and its file
# choosers — they start without a shell and inherit nothing from ~/.zshenv.
#
# Only palette-invariant values belong here — anything that changes with the
# palette needs a fresh login to take effect from this file, and this desk
# switches palette without one. QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME picks the qt6ct platform
# plugin, not a colour scheme; the scheme lives in qt6ct.conf, which
# `,theme.sh` rewrites live, so this line is never the thing standing between
# a switch and the result.
#
# XCURSOR_THEME/SIZE are the exception: they ARE per-palette, and were the one
# genuine next-login value this file held. They stay, but only as a SEED for a
# fresh login before any apply has run. `,theme.sh apply` owns them after that,
# writing all three places a cursor has to reach — `hyprctl setcursor` for the
# running compositor, `systemctl --user set-environment` for apps launched
# afterwards (uwsm app scopes inherit the user manager, not a shell), and this
# file for next time. Without the middle write, a browser opened after a switch
# would still come up with the old cursor.
#
# QT_STYLE_OVERRIDE stays unset: it would override qt6ct.conf's own choice.
QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=qt6ct
XCURSOR_THEME={{ theme_cursor }}
XCURSOR_SIZE={{ theme_cursor_size }}
